WEBVTT

00:00:12.185 --> 00:00:16.146
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log, stardate 58105.1.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:16.189 --> 00:00:18.104
&lt;i&gt;The Pakleds continue
their unprovoked attacks&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:18.148 --> 00:00:19.758
&lt;i&gt;on Federation trade routes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.586
&lt;i&gt;Seeking a cease-fire,
theCerritos&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:21.629 --> 00:00:24.023
&lt;i&gt;is on a diplomatic mission
to the Pakled homeworld,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.417
&lt;i&gt;which they call Pakled Planet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.159
Starfleet Command entrusted me
with this mission

00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:32.640
because of our experience
with the Pakleds last year.

00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:36.296
Negotiating a cease-fire
would be a huge achievement.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.125
If you keep doing Picard-level
peace-brokering like this,

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:40.779
they might give you
an &lt;i&gt;Enterprise.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:42.650
Well, I don't know about that.

00:00:42.694 --> 00:00:44.913
Remember, it's just the Pakleds.

00:00:44.957 --> 00:00:47.002
This shouldn't be
too complicated.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.225
Ambassador Grubdin.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:54.184
Welcome, Captain Janeway.

00:00:54.227 --> 00:00:57.535
Pakled Planet is big and strong.

00:00:57.578 --> 00:01:01.060
Right. Well, I'm actually
Captain Freeman of the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:01.104 --> 00:01:03.106
I'm here to discuss
a cease-fire.

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:04.672
Oh, I was misinformed.

00:01:04.716 --> 00:01:06.848
I do not have
a big enough helmet

00:01:06.892 --> 00:01:08.546
to make cease-fires.

00:01:08.589 --> 00:01:11.897
Okay. Well, then I need to talk
to someone with a bigger helmet.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.334
- Stay back.

00:01:17.642 --> 00:01:19.774
Guys, the prisoner Rumdar.

00:01:19.818 --> 00:01:22.603
He ran away from Pakled Planet
to her ship.

00:01:22.647 --> 00:01:25.824
You! Why did you steal Rumdar?

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:28.043
I can assure you,
we did no such thing.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.611
Ransom,
is there a Pakled on my ship?

00:01:30.655 --> 00:01:32.091
- That's an affirmative, Captain.

00:01:32.135 --> 00:01:34.615
This ship is strong.
I can live here now.

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:37.096
- We think
he's requesting asylum. &lt;i&gt;
No!&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.229
Until she gives Rumdar back,

00:01:39.272 --> 00:01:41.883
Janeway stays here!

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.873
Guys, it's pretty cool
that the captain

00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:01.311
- gets to negotiate peace, right?
- Uh, yeah.

00:03:01.354 --> 00:03:03.661
- I'm sure she's thinking
the same thing.

00:03:03.704 --> 00:03:06.490
Nothing ruins breakfast
like a work assignment.

00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:08.927
Oh, no,
anomaly consolidation duty.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.711
- Oh, yes!
Ugh.

00:03:10.755 --> 00:03:12.365
- I got it, too.
- So did I.

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:15.281
- What's anomaly consolidation?
- You get to go around the ship

00:03:15.325 --> 00:03:16.978
and collect the bridge crew's
research materials

00:03:17.022 --> 00:03:18.980
- from their missions.
- It's trash day.

00:03:19.024 --> 00:03:21.156
It's our bosses, who have
accumulated all sorts of stuff,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.855
saying, "Hey, peons,
come pick up our trash."

00:03:23.898 --> 00:03:26.205
Dangerous science trash
that can't just get recycled

00:03:26.249 --> 00:03:27.815
in a matter recombinator.

00:03:27.859 --> 00:03:29.643
We have to pack it up
and send it to a facility.

00:03:29.687 --> 00:03:31.689
Could be a nice break
from our usual duties.

00:03:31.732 --> 00:03:32.820
Maybe it'll be fun.

00:03:32.864 --> 00:03:34.561
Oh, sweet, sweet Tendi, no.

00:03:34.605 --> 00:03:37.477
ACD is the most degrading day
of the year.

00:03:37.521 --> 00:03:39.305
Don't listen to her.
This is gonna be great.

00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:46.443
Sorry.

00:03:46.486 --> 00:03:47.966
I-It's just the face
that you made.

00:03:48.009 --> 00:03:49.446
I couldn't help it.

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:51.839
Okay, all right.
We're all having so much fun.

00:03:51.883 --> 00:03:53.754
- At my expense.

00:03:53.798 --> 00:03:56.279
Hey. Boimler, right?

00:03:56.322 --> 00:03:58.193
Heard a lot of buzz
about your time on the &lt;i&gt;Titan.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.152
Oh, uh, Ensign Casey. Hi.

00:04:00.195 --> 00:04:02.633
- You guys heard about that?
- You're a legend. Listen,

00:04:02.676 --> 00:04:04.939
we've got this little club where
we help each other rank up,

00:04:04.983 --> 00:04:06.680
and right now
we're down a member.

00:04:06.724 --> 00:04:09.030
P'jok got promoted
to the &lt;i&gt;Ventura.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:09.074 --> 00:04:11.816
- What? No way.
- That's what the Redshirts do.

00:04:11.859 --> 00:04:13.644
We help each other
land promotions.

00:04:13.687 --> 00:04:16.081
One day we'll all be captains.

00:04:16.124 --> 00:04:17.996
You call yourselves Redshirts?

00:04:18.039 --> 00:04:20.607
Cool name, right?
Makes us sound invincible.

00:04:20.651 --> 00:04:22.217
But why would you want me
to be one? I mean, I got

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.350
the red shirt, but is there,
like, a form I need to fill out?

00:04:24.394 --> 00:04:25.830
You served with Riker.

00:04:25.873 --> 00:04:27.832
That kind of experience
is super valuable.

00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:29.834
Listen, there's gonna be
an acting captain's duty

00:04:29.877 --> 00:04:32.445
up for grabs later today.
Only us Redshirts know about it.

00:04:32.489 --> 00:04:34.795
Acting captain?
Like, l-like on the bridge?

00:04:34.839 --> 00:04:36.580
You tell us Riker stuff today,

00:04:36.623 --> 00:04:38.321
I'll get you in the running
for the big chair.

00:04:38.364 --> 00:04:40.061
But...
I have ACD.

00:04:40.105 --> 00:04:41.889
Anomaly duty? No sweat.

00:04:41.933 --> 00:04:44.675
- We'll pull some strings,
get you out of it.
- Uh...

00:04:44.718 --> 00:04:47.025
- I don't know.
It's awesome
that you served

00:04:47.068 --> 00:04:48.766
on the &lt;i&gt;Titan,
but there has to be a reason&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:48.809 --> 00:04:50.115
you're back on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:50.158 --> 00:04:52.204
You don't carry yourself
like a leader.

00:04:52.247 --> 00:04:53.640
We could help you with that.

00:04:53.684 --> 00:04:55.686
- But if you're not interested...

00:04:55.729 --> 00:04:57.252
Uh... wait.

00:04:58.166 --> 00:05:00.168
- I'm in. Let's do this.

00:05:00.212 --> 00:05:02.867
Excelsior.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.479
Unbelievable.
Boimler's cozying up

00:05:06.523 --> 00:05:08.960
with those brownnosers
to get out of trash day?

00:05:09.003 --> 00:05:11.745
- Such a great call.
- More trash for the rest of us.

00:05:11.789 --> 00:05:14.748
- I smell adventure.

00:05:14.792 --> 00:05:16.837
So, what has you seeking asylum?

00:05:16.881 --> 00:05:18.883
Religious persecution?
Leading a rebellion?

00:05:18.926 --> 00:05:20.363
Some sort of sex stuff?

00:05:20.406 --> 00:05:22.669
I want to see
how the shields work.

00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:26.543
You want to see our
top secret defensive schematics?

00:05:26.586 --> 00:05:29.110
Yeah, and your crimson
force field, too.

00:05:29.154 --> 00:05:32.026
Uh, I will see
if it's operational.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.333
You getting "Bazminti when
he pulled back the veil" vibes

00:05:34.377 --> 00:05:36.901
- from this guy?
- Oh, yeah. Captain Freeman?

00:05:36.944 --> 00:05:39.599
Our Pakled refugee appears
to be more of a Pakled spy.

00:05:39.643 --> 00:05:41.949
&lt;i&gt;What?! He hasn't gotten
anything, has he?&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:41.993 --> 00:05:43.951
- No, I think we'll be okay.

00:05:43.995 --> 00:05:46.171
He just took a photo
of his own foot.

00:05:46.214 --> 00:05:48.173
&lt;i&gt;-Hmm, this could work
to our advantage.
- Oh. Ah!&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:48.216 --> 00:05:50.436
&lt;i&gt;Maybe he'll reveal something
about the attacks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.698
&lt;i&gt;Keep him talking.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:51.742 --> 00:05:54.397
- On it.
Oh!

00:05:56.007 --> 00:05:57.965
Ransom's always going
on fun away missions.

00:05:58.009 --> 00:06:00.751
You just know he'll have crazy
anomalies we can check out.

00:06:00.794 --> 00:06:04.232
Oh, great.
A pile of unlabeled crystals.

00:06:04.276 --> 00:06:06.496
You're supposed to keep
stuff like this in a lab.

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:08.062
Ignoring protocol.

00:06:08.106 --> 00:06:09.890
Yeah, one of the perks
of being a commander.

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:13.459
Oh, man!

00:06:13.503 --> 00:06:15.461
Ooh, this is neat.

00:06:15.505 --> 00:06:16.984
You can tell
from the occipital bone

00:06:17.028 --> 00:06:18.812
that this was one big froggy.

00:06:18.856 --> 00:06:20.640
Tendi, whoa, easy.
I think that's from the planet

00:06:20.684 --> 00:06:21.902
where everything evolved
all weird.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.165
Uh...

00:06:24.209 --> 00:06:25.297
Oh!

00:06:26.559 --> 00:06:27.647
- Aah!
Whoa!

00:06:27.691 --> 00:06:29.170
Whoa, Rutherford,
you're blowing up.

00:06:29.214 --> 00:06:31.477
- It's altering his biomatrix!
Whoa, whoa!

00:06:31.521 --> 00:06:32.913
- I got a big ole body.

00:06:32.957 --> 00:06:34.262
- Stop moving around.
- Oh!

00:06:34.306 --> 00:06:35.350
- I can't stop.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.309
I'm big beyond belief. Oh, no!

00:06:37.352 --> 00:06:39.267
Tendi, grab the red vial.

00:06:39.311 --> 00:06:40.617
Got it.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:41.792
Smear that crap on his nose.

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:49.234
Ugh.
- You just experienced

00:06:49.277 --> 00:06:51.410
- full molecular engorgement
in a matter of seconds!

00:06:51.454 --> 00:06:53.020
Did it feel amazing?

00:06:53.064 --> 00:06:55.501
Hey, Boimler, how often
did Riker clean his trombone?

00:06:55.545 --> 00:06:56.676
- Oh!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:57.808
Oh, constantly.

00:06:57.851 --> 00:06:59.157
It was actually
kind of disruptive.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.465
I need to learn
to blow something brass.

00:07:02.508 --> 00:07:03.814
Okay.

00:07:03.857 --> 00:07:05.903
So, that was our
top secret Starfleet gift shop.

00:07:05.946 --> 00:07:09.907
Next, how about we show you the,
uh, high-security juice bar?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.692
No!
Now I want to see the warp core.

00:07:12.736 --> 00:07:14.781
Sure, sure.
We'll get you there, big guy.

00:07:14.825 --> 00:07:16.870
We're not exactly dealing
with the Tal Shiar here.

00:07:16.914 --> 00:07:20.091
Let's see if we can get him
to tell us about their systems.

00:07:21.614 --> 00:07:23.268
Wait.

00:07:23.311 --> 00:07:25.879
Where'd he go?
Computer, locate Pakled refugee.

00:07:25.923 --> 00:07:27.838
&lt;i&gt;No Pakled detected.
- What?&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:27.881 --> 00:07:30.101
Did he leave the ship?
Did he somehow cloak himself?

00:07:30.144 --> 00:07:32.016
&lt;i&gt;-Unknown.
- Zinda, his eyes red.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:32.059 --> 00:07:33.234
I'll check engineering.

00:07:38.718 --> 00:07:41.504
Okay, let's see what
the next awesome anomalies are.

00:07:48.815 --> 00:07:50.513
Um...

00:07:58.608 --> 00:08:00.566
Oh.

00:08:10.794 --> 00:08:12.970
You want a rotten mushfroot?

00:08:13.013 --> 00:08:14.580
Uh, no, thank you.

00:08:14.624 --> 00:08:17.191
I just want to talk cease-fire
with whomever's in charge.

00:08:17.235 --> 00:08:20.543
Oh!
Janeway turned down mushfroot.

00:08:22.414 --> 00:08:26.374
Her Mushesty the queen!

00:08:26.418 --> 00:08:28.551
Ah, Your Highness,
allow me to...

00:08:28.594 --> 00:08:31.118
You can't kill Rumdar.
Rumdar is our prisoner.

00:08:31.162 --> 00:08:32.729
We will kill Rumdar.

00:08:32.772 --> 00:08:34.861
I can assure you,
Rumdar's in good hands.

00:08:34.905 --> 00:08:37.168
Nobody is killing Rumdar.

00:08:37.211 --> 00:08:39.997
Prove it.
I want to talk to Rumdar.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.130
Ransom, put the Pakled refugee
on the line.

00:08:43.174 --> 00:08:46.003
&lt;i&gt;Uh, actually, we've
temporarily lost track of him.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:46.046 --> 00:08:47.352
What?!

00:08:47.395 --> 00:08:49.833
Rumdar is, uh,
in the bathroom.

00:08:49.876 --> 00:08:53.619
But he said that you
should negotiate a cease-fire.

00:08:53.663 --> 00:08:56.622
Oh, I don't have
a big enough helmet to do that.

00:08:56.666 --> 00:08:58.450
Are you me?

00:09:00.017 --> 00:09:01.627
&lt;i&gt;Boimler,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:01.671 --> 00:09:03.063
you need to look like a leader

00:09:03.107 --> 00:09:04.630
if you want people
to treat you like one.

00:09:04.674 --> 00:09:06.632
First,
you've got to fix this posture.

00:09:06.676 --> 00:09:08.068
You're like this

00:09:08.112 --> 00:09:11.115
when you need to be like this.

00:09:11.158 --> 00:09:12.943
Oh, wow.

00:09:12.986 --> 00:09:15.336
I didn't realize
my spine went that far.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.556
- That's new.
- Now, this outfit? Oof.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:19.123
This is not a good look.

00:09:19.166 --> 00:09:21.647
We all wear this.
It's a uniform.

00:09:21.691 --> 00:09:24.302
- The captain literally wears
the same thing, and she's...
- Right now

00:09:24.345 --> 00:09:25.651
this uniform is wearing you.

00:09:25.695 --> 00:09:27.479
Easy to fix
with a few modifications.

00:09:27.522 --> 00:09:30.264
- Ooh, did Riker
modify his uniform?
- What? No.

00:09:30.308 --> 00:09:31.962
I mean, I guess they had to put
a lot of extra room

00:09:32.005 --> 00:09:33.703
in his pants.
For his legs, I mean.

00:09:33.746 --> 00:09:35.269
'Cause he's tall.

00:09:35.313 --> 00:09:36.880
- tall guy, big legs.
- Oh, my God, your hair.

00:09:36.923 --> 00:09:38.533
Wow, I didn't even take in
the hair.

00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:41.145
I like my hair.
I'm a cutie. This is good hair.

00:09:41.188 --> 00:09:43.277
But would you follow it
into battle?

00:09:43.321 --> 00:09:47.107
Maybe just a trim?

00:09:47.151 --> 00:09:49.196
Introducing the new and improved

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.677
Bradward Boimler.

00:09:54.071 --> 00:09:55.986
Oh, I feel amazing.

00:09:56.029 --> 00:09:57.814
Oh, look at these shoulders!
Damn.

00:09:57.857 --> 00:10:00.338
Starfleet royalty.

00:10:00.381 --> 00:10:02.993
- Oh! Aw.
- Aah!

00:10:03.036 --> 00:10:04.777
Boimler?
You look amazing.

00:10:04.821 --> 00:10:06.823
Thank you. The
Redshirts gave me a makeover.

00:10:06.866 --> 00:10:08.563
I-I might have a shot
at acting captain.

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:11.218
Whoa,
is that a Retroovian flask?

00:10:11.262 --> 00:10:12.742
Uh, you know it.

00:10:12.785 --> 00:10:14.265
Careful. Those can release
a gelatinous spray

00:10:14.308 --> 00:10:15.483
- that traps you in this...
Yeah.

00:10:15.527 --> 00:10:17.790
- We know.

00:10:20.097 --> 00:10:21.446
Oh, uh, got to go.
But I want to hear

00:10:21.489 --> 00:10:22.752
everything later.
Watch out for that spray.

00:10:22.795 --> 00:10:25.406
- It'll mess you up.
- Damn it, the Nanobots.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:26.930
Billups can calculate
warp variance,

00:10:26.973 --> 00:10:29.193
but he can't remember to tighten
the lid on a jar.

00:10:29.236 --> 00:10:32.152
Aw, but come on. How often
do we get to be face-to-face

00:10:32.196 --> 00:10:33.850
with these tiny terrors?

00:10:33.893 --> 00:10:36.591
they're not
full-sized robots, right? Right?

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:38.768
Tendi, this stuff
is eating my fingerprints.

00:10:38.811 --> 00:10:42.119
There's no bright side!
Stop trying to make this fun.

00:10:42.162 --> 00:10:43.773
- But...
- What is your deal, okay?

00:10:43.816 --> 00:10:47.254
Every day isn't gonna be some
pristine, exploratory adventure.

00:10:47.298 --> 00:10:48.952
Sometimes it's work,
and it sucks.

00:10:48.995 --> 00:10:50.083
Get used to it!

00:10:50.127 --> 00:10:52.303
Okay. Sorry.

00:10:52.346 --> 00:10:54.000
Where could he be?

00:10:54.044 --> 00:10:56.089
He's giant and brown.

00:10:57.047 --> 00:10:59.614
Being captain
is the role of a lifetime.

00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:02.487
Leader. Fighter.

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:03.836
Lover.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.446
The captain needs
to always be prepared

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.145
to give a rousing speech,
so go ahead.

00:11:08.188 --> 00:11:09.755
[rolls "R"]:
Rouse them.

00:11:09.799 --> 00:11:12.236
Uh, what am I
supposed to speech about?

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:13.367
Ooh! A temporal rift.

00:11:13.411 --> 00:11:14.717
Oh, oh! With a plasma grid.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.283
And the replicators are broken.

00:11:16.327 --> 00:11:19.591
Sounds like a crew
that could use some inspiration.

00:11:19.634 --> 00:11:21.071
Right now?

00:11:21.114 --> 00:11:22.507
Okay. Uh...

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.814
Um, attention, crew. Um,

00:11:24.857 --> 00:11:27.251
I'm your captain.
I'm Captain Boimler.

00:11:27.294 --> 00:11:30.080
Uh, we've got a plasma grid
and a temporal rift.

00:11:30.123 --> 00:11:32.735
Sorry,
you said "temporal rift," right?

00:11:32.778 --> 00:11:34.475
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:11:34.519 --> 00:11:37.914
And, uh, lots of danger.
But as sure as, uh,

00:11:37.957 --> 00:11:41.221
this is my captain's chair, um,

00:11:41.265 --> 00:11:42.919
you can count on me

00:11:42.962 --> 00:11:44.572
'cause I'm your captain.

00:11:44.616 --> 00:11:46.313
Yes, sirree.

00:11:47.314 --> 00:11:48.794
We should mutiny.

00:11:48.838 --> 00:11:50.622
Sorry, sorry, no, no, no.
I know that wasn't good.

00:11:50.665 --> 00:11:53.799
It's just this isn't the same
as actually being on the bridge.

00:11:53.843 --> 00:11:56.323
The bridge is wherever you are.

00:11:56.367 --> 00:11:58.238
Close your eyes,
think about Riker,

00:11:58.282 --> 00:12:01.067
and say what he would say.
From the heart.

00:12:01.111 --> 00:12:03.200
&lt;i&gt;-His&lt;/i&gt; heart.

00:12:03.243 --> 00:12:05.942
Look, I may not know
exactly what we're up against,

00:12:05.985 --> 00:12:08.858
but I do know that in this,
our darkest hour,

00:12:08.901 --> 00:12:10.381
I'm grateful.

00:12:10.424 --> 00:12:14.254
Grateful to have a ship
and a crew I trust with my life.

00:12:14.298 --> 00:12:16.082
Now, I'll be honest.
There's no guarantee

00:12:16.126 --> 00:12:18.389
we're gonna get out of this.
But if we do, it'll be

00:12:18.432 --> 00:12:21.261
because of your combined talent
and dedication.

00:12:21.305 --> 00:12:23.916
It's been the honor of my life
to serve as your captain.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.570
But we're not dead yet,

00:12:25.613 --> 00:12:28.225
so how about we go in
and kick some ass.

00:12:28.268 --> 00:12:30.488
Red alert! Take us in.

00:12:30.531 --> 00:12:33.317
Now,

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:34.927
&lt;i&gt;that&lt;/i&gt; sounds like a captain.

00:12:37.887 --> 00:12:40.628
Wow, even Dr. Migleemo
has stuff?

00:12:40.672 --> 00:12:41.847
I didn't know
he even went on missions.

00:12:41.891 --> 00:12:43.283
That's a pile of random junk.

00:12:43.327 --> 00:12:45.024
- Come on.
Even you have to admit that.
- No.

00:12:45.068 --> 00:12:47.418
And honestly, I'm getting tired
of you guys whining all day.

00:12:47.461 --> 00:12:49.594
If you're so over
anomaly collection,

00:12:49.637 --> 00:12:51.117
then I'll just do it myself.

00:12:51.161 --> 00:12:52.553
- Okay. Works for me.
- Oh, great idea.

00:12:55.426 --> 00:12:57.863
Okay, let's see. There's
this dusty goggles thing.

00:12:57.907 --> 00:13:00.126
Ooh, half of some sort of sword.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.520
- You guys
are really missing out!
Mm-hmm.

00:13:02.563 --> 00:13:04.435
Look, he's throwing out

00:13:04.478 --> 00:13:06.480
a perfectly good storybook.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.184
Oh, it's one
of those energy field books

00:13:14.227 --> 00:13:15.272
that makes stories come to life.

00:13:15.315 --> 00:13:16.621
Come here!

00:13:16.664 --> 00:13:19.276
Get back in this book!

00:13:20.277 --> 00:13:21.278
- Oh!

00:13:21.321 --> 00:13:23.367
Huh?

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.848
- Oh, no.

00:13:25.891 --> 00:13:27.284
- Uh...
- Crap, crap, crap!
- Slug!

00:13:27.327 --> 00:13:29.808
- No!

00:13:29.852 --> 00:13:32.637
- Tendi!
- Ugh! Okay, we just got to find
the right hypospray.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:33.943
- Uh, hang tight, Tendi!

00:13:33.986 --> 00:13:35.945
Don't get digested!

00:13:35.988 --> 00:13:38.991
- Uh, uh... Ha!

00:13:45.171 --> 00:13:47.173
- Ugh.

00:13:50.089 --> 00:13:52.004
- Oh, my gosh. Are you okay?
- D'Vana?

00:13:52.048 --> 00:13:55.312
You were right.

00:13:55.355 --> 00:13:58.793
Anomaly consolidation day &lt;i&gt;
is&lt;/i&gt; the worst.

00:13:58.837 --> 00:14:00.839
Hey, we've all...
I mean, who among us

00:14:00.883 --> 00:14:03.015
hasn't been pooped out
by an alien creature?

00:14:03.059 --> 00:14:04.887
- It is not a...
- Don't touch me!

00:14:06.976 --> 00:14:09.369
Captain, this is going sideways.

00:14:09.413 --> 00:14:11.284
I recommend we beam out now.

00:14:11.328 --> 00:14:12.851
No. We have to make this work,

00:14:12.895 --> 00:14:15.506
or it'll turn into a big, brown,
Pakled smear on my record.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.945
I am King Pakled.

00:14:19.989 --> 00:14:23.035
- Finally. It is an honor
to meet you, sir.

00:14:24.123 --> 00:14:27.648
I am emperor of the Pakleds.

00:14:27.692 --> 00:14:31.130
- Okay. Well, then,
it's an honor to m...

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.482
Rebelution!

00:14:45.536 --> 00:14:47.581
The big-helmeted Pakleds

00:14:47.625 --> 00:14:50.019
will no longer control us!

00:14:50.062 --> 00:14:51.585
Ooh.

00:14:51.629 --> 00:14:55.198
I am now Pakled leader.

00:14:55.241 --> 00:14:57.983
Behold my giant helmet!

00:14:58.027 --> 00:14:59.811
- He is strong.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.168
You know, I was
a little skeptical at first,

00:15:09.212 --> 00:15:11.518
but I really am feeling
way more captainy than usual.

00:15:11.562 --> 00:15:13.999
- Now you have to start
living like one, too.
- Oh, you mean,

00:15:14.043 --> 00:15:15.740
like sitting in a centered chair
all day or...?

00:15:15.783 --> 00:15:18.221
Nothing tells you about
a captain more than the officers

00:15:18.264 --> 00:15:19.787
they've chosen to have
at their side.

00:15:19.831 --> 00:15:21.267
That's true in your social life

00:15:21.311 --> 00:15:23.269
- as much as it is on the bridge.
- Oh.

00:15:23.313 --> 00:15:25.445
I've got that covered.
My friends are awesome.

00:15:25.489 --> 00:15:26.838
Look, that's them right there.

00:15:28.622 --> 00:15:30.973
They've been
consolidating anomalies all day.

00:15:31.016 --> 00:15:33.714
- It's pretty cool, right?
- No, not cool.

00:15:33.758 --> 00:15:35.325
Those three
are always elbow-deep

00:15:35.368 --> 00:15:36.979
in some kind of slime.

00:15:37.022 --> 00:15:39.024
Yeah, we work in Starfleet.
I mean, slime's a given.

00:15:39.068 --> 00:15:41.679
No, &lt;i&gt;we&lt;/i&gt; work in Starfleet.

00:15:41.722 --> 00:15:43.333
- They work &lt;i&gt;for&lt;/i&gt; Starfleet.

00:15:43.376 --> 00:15:46.075
Okay, hold on. They're
the same rank as you or me.

00:15:46.118 --> 00:15:47.815
And while we've been
"playing captain" all day,

00:15:47.859 --> 00:15:49.687
they've been doing real work
to help the ship.

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:52.081
This isn't a friendship.
It's a starship.

00:15:52.124 --> 00:15:53.169
Are you a star

00:15:53.212 --> 00:15:55.171
- or not?
- What?

00:15:55.214 --> 00:15:56.868
The bridge crew
brought in this crap,

00:15:56.911 --> 00:15:58.957
&lt;i&gt;they&lt;/i&gt; should clean it up.
I'm not their mom.

00:15:59.001 --> 00:16:01.220
Uh, I don't know.
It's not that bad.

00:16:01.264 --> 00:16:03.788
It was the worst!
I hate this stupid ship.

00:16:03.831 --> 00:16:06.269
Whoa,
you love the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:06.312 --> 00:16:08.053
Ugh,
I must have sounded so stupid.

00:16:08.097 --> 00:16:09.794
I thought
we were gonna have so much fun

00:16:09.837 --> 00:16:11.100
picking up the trash.

00:16:11.143 --> 00:16:13.537
Ha!
I even volunteered us for it.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.408
- Wait, you did?
- Why?

00:16:15.452 --> 00:16:17.454
You guys were always sad that
we don't go on cool missions.

00:16:17.497 --> 00:16:18.977
So Ensign Genius over here

00:16:19.021 --> 00:16:20.022
figured it would be fun

00:16:20.065 --> 00:16:21.545
to get closer to the action.

00:16:21.588 --> 00:16:23.329
But you guys were right.
It sucked!

00:16:23.373 --> 00:16:24.939
And being lower decks sucks!

00:16:24.983 --> 00:16:27.072
I wish I was still on Orion!

00:16:27.116 --> 00:16:28.595
Uh, Tendi,
that cube's kind of...

00:16:28.639 --> 00:16:30.771
Today has been
totally degrading!

00:16:30.815 --> 00:16:32.991
Uh, maybe-maybe put down
the cube before you...

00:16:39.084 --> 00:16:40.912
- We got a scorpion here!

00:16:40.955 --> 00:16:42.348
What was that cube?

00:16:42.392 --> 00:16:43.741
There has to be a way
to reverse it.

00:16:44.698 --> 00:16:46.396
I'm getting tired of you guys

00:16:46.439 --> 00:16:48.789
whining all day!

00:17:02.629 --> 00:17:03.891
Is that Tendi?

00:17:04.892 --> 00:17:06.242
We got to do something.

00:17:06.285 --> 00:17:08.635
You're right.
The crew depends on us.

00:17:08.679 --> 00:17:12.422
The Starfleet manual
defines "danger" as "a force

00:17:12.465 --> 00:17:15.164
- which causes
or tends to cause harm."
- It is in times of doubt...

00:17:15.207 --> 00:17:17.253
- A ship that encounters
no rough wind

00:17:17.296 --> 00:17:19.211
is a ship
that's never sailed at all.

00:17:19.255 --> 00:17:20.995
Are any of you
actually gonna do something?

00:17:21.039 --> 00:17:23.172
We're doing it.
We're inspiring the crew.

00:17:23.215 --> 00:17:25.174
We &lt;i&gt;are&lt;/i&gt; the crew!

00:17:25.217 --> 00:17:27.437
Tendi,

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.265
I know you're in there.
You're gonna be okay.

00:17:32.181 --> 00:17:33.617
What happened?

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.097
Did she touch a mysterious orb?

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:36.489
What? No. It was a cube.

00:17:36.533 --> 00:17:38.100
Oh! Uh, I bet it was
an Ataxian mood shifter.

00:17:38.143 --> 00:17:39.362
I've got this.

00:17:39.405 --> 00:17:41.451
Computer, big bowl of beans,

00:17:41.494 --> 00:17:42.974
hot.

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:47.239
Hey, Tendi. Whoa! I sure hope

00:17:47.283 --> 00:17:49.633
I don't spill these beans
on my...

00:17:49.676 --> 00:17:51.722
Aah! Aah, God.

00:17:53.637 --> 00:17:55.378
Computer,
birthday cake, lit candles,

00:17:55.421 --> 00:17:57.031
various temperatures.

00:17:57.075 --> 00:17:58.946
Wow.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.166
It sure is hard
carrying this birthday cake

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:03.777
with all this bean slime
on my...

00:18:03.821 --> 00:18:06.302
- What the hell is he doing?

00:18:06.345 --> 00:18:07.520
- Shut up. Look.

00:18:07.564 --> 00:18:09.174
Oh, no, and now the candles

00:18:09.218 --> 00:18:11.307
have lit my uniform on fire.
What a predicament.

00:18:14.048 --> 00:18:16.138
It's working.

00:18:16.181 --> 00:18:17.791
Her emotional armor
is weakening.

00:18:21.186 --> 00:18:22.970
Computer, taffy, honey, shrimp,

00:18:23.014 --> 00:18:24.494
soda, corn, steak,
chicken nugget,

00:18:24.537 --> 00:18:25.886
crispy lemon rock candy,

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:27.888
chili, gravy,
chocolate sundae! Hot!

00:18:34.417 --> 00:18:37.594
That was such a waste
of reassembled proteins.

00:18:37.637 --> 00:18:39.465
It really was.

00:18:39.509 --> 00:18:41.728
You okay?
- Yeah.

00:18:41.772 --> 00:18:43.208
Geez,
I was really out of control.

00:18:43.252 --> 00:18:44.688
Thanks for saving me.

00:18:44.731 --> 00:18:47.778
Oh, of course.
That's what we do.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.134
Oh, no. How long were we out?

00:18:56.178 --> 00:18:57.570
Rumdar could be anywhere.

00:18:57.614 --> 00:18:59.442
We never should have
underestimated him.

00:18:59.485 --> 00:19:01.313
Shaka?

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:06.275
Maybe we didn't
underestimate him.

00:19:07.319 --> 00:19:10.061
Holy

00:19:10.104 --> 00:19:12.890
I don't know how he was able to
survive in the vacuum of space,

00:19:12.933 --> 00:19:16.502
- but he's totally fine.
- Uh, Pakleds are strong.

00:19:16.546 --> 00:19:18.983
How did you get outside
in the first place?

00:19:19.026 --> 00:19:22.204
I went to the bathroom.
When I pressed the flush button,

00:19:22.247 --> 00:19:24.771
I got shot
out of a little hatch.

00:19:24.815 --> 00:19:26.425
Are you sure
you weren't in an air lock?

00:19:26.469 --> 00:19:29.602
Can I have all your codes now?

00:19:29.646 --> 00:19:32.779
Get him out of here.

00:19:35.304 --> 00:19:37.697
Janeway, die! Janeway, die!

00:19:37.741 --> 00:19:40.831
Ah, Rumdar returns.

00:19:40.874 --> 00:19:43.486
Hi, everybody.

00:19:43.529 --> 00:19:44.922
We tricked you, Janeway.

00:19:44.965 --> 00:19:46.445
We never wanted peace.

00:19:46.489 --> 00:19:49.361
Rumdar was a spy.

00:19:49.405 --> 00:19:51.145
What did you learn, spy?

00:19:51.189 --> 00:19:53.974
The &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt; has
the biggest bathrooms ever,

00:19:54.018 --> 00:19:56.412
and she is not Captain Janeway.

00:19:56.455 --> 00:19:58.196
- She is Captain Freeman!

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.633
- That's what
I've been telling you.

00:20:00.677 --> 00:20:02.679
I tricked you.

00:20:02.722 --> 00:20:05.682
And I didn't give up
any information, either.

00:20:05.725 --> 00:20:07.336
I'm a good spy.

00:20:07.379 --> 00:20:10.730
Well, yes, you are amazing.

00:20:10.774 --> 00:20:13.690
I just wish I knew
what information you kept secret

00:20:13.733 --> 00:20:16.301
so I could know
how amazing you are.

00:20:16.345 --> 00:20:19.130
I didn't tell you anything
about our big plan

00:20:19.173 --> 00:20:21.872
to smuggle a Varuvian bomb
onto Earth.

00:20:21.915 --> 00:20:23.656
- Is that right?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:28.270
Oh, Rumdar,
you truly are a master spy.

00:20:28.313 --> 00:20:30.315
Two to beam up.

00:20:32.099 --> 00:20:33.884
Wait a minute.

00:20:33.927 --> 00:20:36.800
You just beat Captain Janeway!

00:20:36.843 --> 00:20:40.369
Rumdar! Rumdar!

00:20:43.633 --> 00:20:46.592
Sorry I requested
anomaly consolidation duty

00:20:46.636 --> 00:20:48.986
- and, you know,
went all scorpion.
- Don't apologize.

00:20:49.029 --> 00:20:50.857
The truth is,
collecting weird space crap

00:20:50.901 --> 00:20:52.555
&lt;i&gt;is&lt;/i&gt; part of the fun
of Starfleet.

00:20:52.598 --> 00:20:54.470
Ah, we were kind of being punks
all day.

00:20:54.513 --> 00:20:56.123
We should have fed off
your enthusiasm,

00:20:56.167 --> 00:20:57.951
not tried to tamp it down.

00:20:57.995 --> 00:20:59.779
Yeah, you know what?
The best anomaly today

00:20:59.823 --> 00:21:01.346
was all your silver linings.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:04.088
- And that skull thing.
- Aw, thanks, guys.

00:21:04.131 --> 00:21:05.872
Oh, I still smell

00:21:05.916 --> 00:21:07.874
like slug-digested scorpion,
don't I?

00:21:07.918 --> 00:21:10.094
Yeah. The smell of adventure.

00:21:12.096 --> 00:21:15.055
Whoever Ransom picks,
remember to keep your cool.

00:21:15.099 --> 00:21:16.579
I don't want
anyone freaking out.

00:21:16.622 --> 00:21:19.364
Sorry, you can't come with us.

00:21:19.408 --> 00:21:20.974
That move you pulled
in the mess hall

00:21:21.018 --> 00:21:23.063
- proves you don't belong
in the Redshirts.
- Hey.

00:21:23.107 --> 00:21:25.457
- My friend was in trouble.
- You made a fool of yourself

00:21:25.501 --> 00:21:27.807
to make a bug laugh.
It was shameful.

00:21:27.851 --> 00:21:29.243
All right,
you know what's shameful?

00:21:29.287 --> 00:21:31.376
Trying to build a persona
by copying other captains.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:33.378
You think Riker did that?

00:21:33.422 --> 00:21:35.815
You guys are wasting your time
on this Redshirt stuff.

00:21:35.859 --> 00:21:38.252
- Be your own captains.

00:21:38.296 --> 00:21:40.254
Cute speech.
I'm sure it'll play great

00:21:40.298 --> 00:21:43.519
on the lower decks.
Come on, guys.

00:21:43.562 --> 00:21:46.522
- Guys?
- I, um, I think I'm gonna

00:21:46.565 --> 00:21:49.568
take a break from the Redshirts,
focus on my duties.

00:21:49.612 --> 00:21:50.743
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:21:50.787 --> 00:21:52.615
Fine. I'll try to remember you

00:21:52.658 --> 00:21:54.704
when I'm boldly going
and you're not.

00:21:54.747 --> 00:21:57.707
Sir, I'd like to nominate myself
for the acting captain position.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.969
- Huh?
- I'm the best candidate

00:21:59.012 --> 00:22:00.753
to lead the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; to victory.

00:22:00.797 --> 00:22:02.538
Oh. I don't care. Sure.

00:22:02.581 --> 00:22:04.278
Oh, my God, really? Sir,

00:22:04.322 --> 00:22:06.716
thank you.
Sir, I won't let you down.

00:22:06.759 --> 00:22:09.066
Quick thinking
in the mess today, Mr. Boimler.

00:22:09.109 --> 00:22:10.546
You showed some real leadership.

00:22:10.589 --> 00:22:12.243
Thank you, sir.

00:22:12.286 --> 00:22:15.507
Hey, do you want to catch
a Winger Bingston show sometime?

00:22:15.551 --> 00:22:17.335
Now, that guy
can deliver a speech.

00:22:17.379 --> 00:22:18.554
You ever see his one-man show

00:22:18.597 --> 00:22:19.816
where he played
all of Jupiter's moons?

00:22:19.859 --> 00:22:22.558
Just got off the comms
with Starfleet.

00:22:22.601 --> 00:22:24.168
Sounds like we did a great job.

00:22:24.211 --> 00:22:27.214
- I think that deserves a drink.
- Count me in.

00:22:27.258 --> 00:22:30.304
- Acting Captain,
you have the conn.

00:22:39.226 --> 00:22:41.403
New shift on deck.
Get out of my chair!

00:22:41.446 --> 00:22:43.579
Aah! Thank you.
This-this was a great honor.

00:22:43.622 --> 00:22:45.755
Go clean up Air Lock 17.

00:22:45.798 --> 00:22:48.410
Pakled did something unspeakable
in there.

00:22:48.453 --> 00:22:49.889
Yes, sir.

00:22:52.588 --> 00:22:54.067
&lt;i&gt;Ooh! And then&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:54.111 --> 00:22:55.939
he deflated back
into regular-sized Rutherford.

00:22:55.982 --> 00:22:58.898
Big-body Rutherford?
Aw, I missed all the good stuff.

00:22:58.942 --> 00:23:00.291
Not &lt;i&gt;all&lt;/i&gt; the good stuff.

00:23:00.334 --> 00:23:02.032
Snagged this baby
from Shaxs's pile.

00:23:02.075 --> 00:23:04.817
Oh, no way. This is
a submanifold casting stone.

00:23:04.861 --> 00:23:06.819
- A what?
- We can use it

00:23:06.863 --> 00:23:08.168
to broadcast our voices
to other planets.

00:23:08.212 --> 00:23:09.648
- What's that good for?

00:23:09.692 --> 00:23:10.823
Yeah, like,
what are we gonna do?

00:23:10.867 --> 00:23:12.869
Prank call Armus?

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:20.354
I wish I had someone to torture.

00:23:20.398 --> 00:23:22.444
&lt;i&gt;Hey, Armus!
Shut up, shut up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:22.487 --> 00:23:25.142
&lt;i&gt;You, uh,
you look like a big bag of crap.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:25.185 --> 00:23:26.970
Who said that? Show yourself.

00:23:27.013 --> 00:23:29.973
I am Armus. This is my domain.

00:23:30.016 --> 00:23:31.888
&lt;i&gt;Yeah, we already know
you're Armus, dummy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:31.931 --> 00:23:33.063
&lt;i&gt;Come and find us.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:33.106 --> 00:23:34.630
&lt;i&gt;We're touching your stuff.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:34.673 --> 00:23:35.892
What stuff? Stop that!

00:23:35.935 --> 00:23:38.198
When I find you,
I'm gonna kill you

00:23:38.242 --> 00:23:39.939
with a flake of my power!

00:23:39.983 --> 00:23:42.942
